      "explanation": [
        "Charge creation validates Money before lookup, hashes the original decimal representation and replays a stored creation response. A duplicate-key race is handled by finding a winning record after a DataIntegrityViolationException; the database schema declares key uniqueness.",
        "Equal numeric values spelled as 10 and 10.00 can identify different requests because the hash uses the original scale. This is a derived static scenario, not an executed test. All integrity violations enter the same recovery branch; key lifetime, caller/provider scope, canonicalization, commit visibility and concurrent different-body requests need explicit policy."
      ],
